en:
That alone is hell.
Plenty of guys can't take it and quit.
But compared to that camp, it's heaven.{p}

The training they gave Akasaka was brutal, even in the other first-years' eyes.
Even when his face swelled up bright red, even when he coughed up blood, they didn't stop.
And then when he went down, they'd yell at him that he had no guts, that he hadn't trained enough.{p}

Of course, the other first-years got way more than their share of hazing, too.
So some of them ran off.
One day, a few of the first-years got together and talked about running away.{p}

None of Hatanaka's bunch ever went near that place.
Well, of course they couldn't.
They didn't want to go there and have something happen.{p}

After practice that day, he went to wipe off his sweat, and what do you know: lying there by his towel was a pair of really grimy gloves.
He didn't know whose they were, but they sure weren't his.
Who on earth...{p}

"...Now, hit me with them, please."
Everyone was dumbfounded.
They were terrified by both things at once: Akasaka, who was supposed to be dead, standing right there, and Hatanaka, screaming just from having the gloves put on him.{p}

They were found not long after that.
The seniors went looking for Hatanaka and the others when they never showed up at the makeshift ring.
Hatanaka and the others weren't at the makeshift ring at all.{p}

One of the seniors foamed at the mouth and collapsed, then went limp and stopped moving.
"Hey, Akasaka, this senior... he isn't dead, is he...?"
By the time one of them noticed, it was too late.{p}

They say the hazing Akasaka and the others dished out was even harsher than in years past.
By the end of the first term, fewer than ten of them were left.
And at last, the annual summer training camp began.{p}

After the first-years were gone, who the hell were Akasaka and the others carrying on that brutal camp with?
Those guys...
They survived, but they say they were never in any shape to box again.{p}

What one of the seniors pointed at was the punching bag.
{a}, I'm not making this up.
Those boxing club guys burned Akasaka's body and hid his bones inside the punching bag.{p}

Ever since that incident, our school's boxing club has been on the skids.
So I hear there's no more hazing like back in those days.
And they don't set any records anymore, either.{p}

I hear their punching bag feels real nice to hit...
That's as far as my story goes.
So, who's telling the next one...?{p}

Yeah, he went back to check.
And sure enough, the gloves were there.
Then he felt an overwhelming urge to put them on.{p}

The gloves fit Hatanaka's hands perfectly.
As if they'd been made just for him.
Feeling kind of strange, Hatanaka decided to head back to the others with them still on.{p}

And then...
"Hatanaka... what've you got on your hands...★"
At his classmate's words, Hatanaka looked down at his hands, and what he saw was...{p}

"Let's stop this.
Before there are any more victims..."
When I said that, the other two suddenly glared at me.{p}

That night, I had a sad dream.
A dream where the people I knew disappeared one by one.
Sometimes it was my seniors in the newspaper club, sometimes my best friend.{p}
